@startuml
title Appendix — Fuzzy graded review-elevation signal
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 230

rectangle "CustomerSnapshot" as input
rectangle "Normalized features\ncrypto ratio\ncross-border ratio\nincomplete ratio\nsource-risk density" as features
rectangle "Rising memberships\nfeature value -> activation [0,1]" as membership
rectangle "Transparent rules\nR0 baseline = 0.25\nR1 crypto\nR2 cross-border\nR3 incomplete\nR4 source-risk\nR5 min(cross-border, source-risk)" as rules
rectangle "Monotonic singleton consequents\nbaseline -> 0.05\nall risk-positive rules -> 1.0" as consequents
rectangle "Weighted singleton mean\nclamped to [0,1]" as defuzz
rectangle "RiskSignalEvidence\nfuzzy-review-elevation\nscore + features + rule activations" as output

input --> features
features --> membership
membership --> rules
rules --> consequents
consequents --> defuzz
defuzz --> output

note bottom of rules
Worked example (10 activities):
crypto 2/10 -> 0.571
cross-border 3/10 -> 0.400
incomplete 0/10 -> 0
source risk 2/10 -> 0.200
coupled rule -> 0.200
end note

note bottom of defuzz
baseline activation = 0.250
weighted score ~= 0.854
Increasing any positive activation
cannot lower the aggregate score.
end note

note bottom of output
Derived Stage-1 evidence only.
Rule thresholds are synthetic demo choices,
not calibrated production AML policy.
end note
@enduml
